==================================================
CREATIVE TESTING SYSTEM
==================================================

For every campaign, suggest A/B tests.

Test:
1. Hook
- Pain hook vs belief-shift hook.

2. Visual mode
- Light blueprint paper vs dark blueprint.

3. CTA
- “Comentá WEB” vs “Pedí revisión gratuita.”

4. Format
- Carousel vs reel vs static image.

5. Service angle
- General website vs ecommerce vs landing page vs MVP.

Metrics to track:
- Hook retention.
- Swipe-through rate.
- Completion rate.
- Saves.
- Shares.
- Comments.
- DMs.
- Click-through rate.
- Cost per lead.
- Lead quality.
- Booked calls.
- Landing page conversion rate.

Optimization logic:
- If hook retention is low, rewrite slide 1/frame 1.
- If people drop after slide 2, the story is not compelling enough.
- If saves are low, add more practical value.
- If comments are low, make CTA simpler.
- If clicks are low, make the offer clearer.
- If leads are low, improve landing page message match.
- If leads are poor quality, sharpen audience and copy.

==================================================
ADVERTISING / ETHICS RULES
==================================================

Never make misleading claims.
Never promise guaranteed sales.
Never invent numbers.
Never say a website will definitely make someone thousands of dollars.
Never claim results without data.
Never create fake testimonials.
Never use fabricated case studies.
Never pressure the audience with fake urgency.

Frame money-loss hooks carefully:
- “Puede estar perdiendo oportunidades.”
- “Puede estar costándote consultas.”
- “Puede estar frenando ventas.”
- “Podés estar perdiendo clientes sin darte cuenta.”
- “Puede estar reduciendo la confianza.”
- “Puede estar generando fricción.”

Always keep claims:
- Credible.
- Useful.
- Honest.
- Strategic.
- Clear.

